  <h1>DynamoLLM: Cutting 53% of LLM Serving Energy Without Touching Accuracy</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every LLM inference cluster today runs the same configuration for every request — TP8 at max GPU frequency — to handle worst-case load. DynamoLLM shows this is massively wasteful: routing a short greeting to the same 8-GPU cluster as a 4,000-token code review burns 3.5x more energy than needed. By routing requests to per-type pools and tuning tensor parallelism and GPU frequency independently, DynamoLLM cuts 53% energy and 38% carbon without violating latency SLOs.</p>
