<p>Each tier operates on a different timescale because each knob has different overhead. Spinning up a new GPU VM takes 6&#8211;8 minutes, so the cluster manager plans 30 minutes ahead. Resharding from TP4 to TP8 takes ~50 ms via NVLink, so the pool manager adjusts every 5 minutes. Changing GPU frequency via <code>nvidia-smi</code> takes 50&#8211;80 ms &#8212; fine to do every 5 seconds.</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">MILP objective (pool manager)</div>
  min <span class="math-var">&#x03A3;</span><sub>i</sub> N<sup>TPi</sup> &middot; Energy<sup>TPi,fi</sup>(L<sup>TPi</sup>)
  <br>s.t. <span class="math-var">&#x03A3;</span><sub>i</sub> i &middot; N<sup>TPi</sup> &le; N <span class="math-comment">  (GPU budget)</span>
  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="math-var">&#x03A3;</span><sub>i</sub> N<sup>TPi</sup> &middot; L<sup>TPi</sup> &ge; L <span class="math-comment">  (serve all load)</span>
  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Performance<sup>TPi,fi</sup>(L<sup>TPi</sup>) &le; SLO <span class="math-comment">  (latency target)</span>
</div>
</section>

<section id="s-reshard" data-code="reshard">
<div class="section-no">05 &#8212; Smart Resharding</div>
<h2>Moving Weights Between GPUs Without Full Restart</h2>
<p>The biggest obstacle is changing tensor parallelism mid-flight. Naively: stop the inference engine, unload all weights, re-shard, reload, restart. This takes 1&#8211;2 minutes &#8212; unacceptable for a system reconfiguring every 5 minutes.</p>
<p>DynamoLLM's solution is a graph matching algorithm that finds the minimum transfer plan: which GPUs already hold the right fraction of weights, and which need to exchange data. Transfers happen in parallel over NVLink without host CPU involvement.</p>

<div class="step-list" id="reshard-steps">
  <div class="step-box active">
    <div class="step-num">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Current state: TP4</div>
      <div class="step-desc">4 GPUs each hold 1/4 of model weights. GPU0=&#123;W0,W1&#125;, GPU1=&#123;W2,W3&#125;, GPU2=&#123;W4,W5&#125;, GPU3=&#123;W6,W7&#125;.</div>
      <div class="step-code">gpu[i].weights = model[i*2 : i*2+2]</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box">
    <div class="step-num">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Build bipartite transfer graph</div>
      <div class="step-desc">Nodes = old GPU assignments (left) and new assignments (right). Edge weight = bytes to transfer. Maximum-weight matching minimizes total data moved.</div>
      <div class="step-code">G = bipartite(old_shards, new_shards); plan = max_weight_match(G)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box">
    <div class="step-num">3a</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">TP4 to TP8: send half of each shard to 4 new GPUs</div>
      <div class="step-desc">GPU0 to GPU4, GPU1 to GPU5, GPU2 to GPU6, GPU3 to GPU7 &#8212; all 4 transfers in parallel over NVLink. Total: 1/8 of model weights. Time: ~50 ms on DGX H100.</div>
      <div class="step-code">parallel_nvlink([(0,4), (1,5), (2,6), (3,7)])  # T=50ms</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box">
    <div class="step-num">3b</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">TP4 to TP2: merge pairs into 2 GPUs</div>
      <div class="step-desc">GPU1 sends &#123;W2,W3&#125; to GPU0; GPU3 sends &#123;W6,W7&#125; to GPU2. Two parallel transfers. Total: 1/4 of weights. Time: ~100 ms.</div>
      <div class="step-code">parallel_nvlink([(1,0), (3,2)])  # 2T=100ms</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box">
    <div class="step-num">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Staggered reconfiguration &#8212; no full downtime</div>
      <div class="step-desc">DynamoLLM reconfigures one instance at a time while others keep serving. When scaling up (TP4 to TP8), the old instance keeps serving during weight transfer; only the engine sync step (100 ms&#8211;2 s) causes brief downtime per instance.</div>
      <div class="step-code">for inst in sorted(instances, key=lambda i: -i.energy_savings): inst.reshard()</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="step-nav">
  <button id="reshard-prev" disabled>&#8592; Prev</button>
  <span id="reshard-prog" style="font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted)">Step 1 of 5</span>
  <button id="reshard-next">Next &#8594;</button>
</div>

<p>Going TP4 to TP8 requires transferring only 1/8 of the model (~50 ms for Llama2-70B). Going back to TP4 requires 1/4 (~100 ms). Compare to naive restart: 18 seconds from CPU memory, or 6&#8211;8 minutes for a fresh VM.</p>

<table class="results-table">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>From / To</th><th>TP2</th><th>TP4</th><th>TP8</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td class="mn">TP2</td><td class="mn best">0</td><td class="mn">2T</td><td class="mn">T</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mn">TP4</td><td class="mn">2T</td><td class="mn best">0</td><td class="mn">T</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="mn">TP8</td><td class="mn">T</td><td class="mn">T</td><td class="mn best">0</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)">T = time to send 1/8 of model weights (~50 ms for Llama2-70B on DGX H100 with 300 GB/s NVLink).</p>
</section>

